WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:05.460
More than 30 years have passed since the release
of the original Child's Play, and Chucky has

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:07.820
remained in the public consciousness ever
since.

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:12.210
But everything old must be new again, and
the killer doll is finally stepping up to

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:13.100
the reboot plate.

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:15.880
What do you need to know before seeing the
new movie?

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:21.040
In the first Child's Play movie from 1988,
the killer doll named Chucky starts out as

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:23.550
a humble murderer of the non-doll variety.

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:28.090
During the first two acts of his life, Chucky
lived as Charles Lee Ray, otherwise known

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:29.990
as "The Lakeshore Strangler."

00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:35.170
Ray was a relatively unremarkable crime enthusiast
distinguished by an interest in voodoo.

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:39.440
In the opening scene, Ray is mortally wounded
by a police officer while fleeing a robbery.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:44.739
In a last act of desperation, he uses his
voodoo expertise to transfer his soul into

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:46.080
a "Good Guy" doll.

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:51.160
(voodoo curse)

00:00:56.690 --> 00:01:00.340
The longer his consciousness stays inside
the doll, the more attached he becomes to

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:02.100
its creepy plastic form.

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:06.780
Hi, I'm Andy, what's your name?"

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:11.260
"Hi, I'm Chucky, and I'm your friend 'til
the end."

00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:16.280
Though he'd spend the next three decades waffling
on whether he wanted to remain a doll, Ray's

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:20.149
first couple of adventures found him trying
to put his soul into another human body and

00:01:20.149 --> 00:01:23.120
stabbing some revenge into anyone that got
in his way.

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:27.880
For the 2019 Child's Play reboot, the voodoo
angle seems to have been scrapped.

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:32.499
This time around, Chucky is being presented
as a "Buddi" doll, an animatronic smart toy

00:01:32.499 --> 00:01:35.479
for a new generation of Facebook and iPhone
users.

00:01:35.479 --> 00:01:38.170
According to Paste, director Lars Klevberg
says,

00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:40.360
"[He's an] out of control robot doll."

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:43.720
"Introducing your new best friend."

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:48.600
With its distrustful take on modern technology,
the new Child's Play sounds like it's going

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:51.160
for a distinctly Black Mirror kind of vibe.

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:56.360
Chucky even uses WiFi-connected smart devices
like drones to assist in much of the mayhem.

00:01:56.369 --> 00:01:59.959
It's certainly a departure from the enchanted
revenge toy we've all come to know over the

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:00.460
years.

00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:04.860
Whether fans of the old movies will be on
board with this new Chucky remains to be seen.

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:10.200
In all seven of the original Chucky movies,
the killer doll was played by acclaimed character

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:14.560
actor Brad Dourif, who also also portrays
Wormtongue in the Lord of the Rings movies,

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:16.380
and Doc Cochran on Deadwood.

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:19.180
"He made the funniest face when I drilled
him."

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:21.740
"Did you see the steam when I sliced open
his guts?"

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:26.660
2019 marks the first time a Chucky movie hasn't
used Dourif's voice.

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:29.660
Instead, the studio enlisted Mark Hamill for
the job.

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:34.090
Beyond playing Luke Skywalker, Hamill has
become one of the most successful voice actors

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:38.280
in Hollywood, memorably voicing the Joker
on Batman: The Animated Series.

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:42.950
And here's where things start to get a little
bit meta: He even played Charles Lee Ray on

00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:45.880
an episode of Robot Chicken back in 2005.

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:47.640
"Hee hee hee hee, who's there?

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:48.900
Come and get some!"

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:54.740
Brad Dourif voiced Chucky in all seven of
the original films, and creator Don Mancini

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:58.340
wrote or co-wrote every entry in the series,
directing three of them.

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:01.860
Producer David Kirschner was also involved
in all of the films.

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:05.570
But eagle-eyed viewers will notice that not
one of these names appears in the credits

00:03:05.570 --> 00:03:07.500
for 2019's Child's Play.

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:08.300
What's the deal with that?

00:03:08.530 --> 00:03:13.360
As it turns out, the reboot is happening against
the wishes of the original creators of Child's

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:13.860
Play.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:17.780
Mancini even requested that his name not be
included in the film's credits.

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:22.740
In a 2018 interview with the Post Mortem podcast,
he described how difficult it was to keep

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:26.810
the franchise going for 30 years, only to
have it pulled out from under him.

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:28.660
"Obviously my feelings were hurt."

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:34.880
The ill will reportedly runs much deeper than
that: Jennifer Tilly, the titular Bride of

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:38.250
Chucky, even started a "Not My Chucky" campaign
on Twitter.

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:41.880
For fans of the original Child's Play franchise,
there's still good news.

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:46.120
Due to some legal loopholes, the rights to
Chucky are astonishingly murky.

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:50.100
As a result, Mancini plans to continue his
Chucky stories in a TV series in the near

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:50.600
future.

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:54.680
Chucky has gone through a number of changes
over the years, but there's one thing that's

00:03:54.690 --> 00:03:56.440
certainly been consistent throughout the films.

00:03:56.440 --> 00:04:00.400
When the cameras start rolling, animatronics
are the star of the show.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:04.540
Naturally, when word got out that a reboot
was in the works, fans were nervous at the

00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:09.200
prospect of an all-CGI murder doll trying
to take the place of their beloved psychotic

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:09.700
puppet.

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:14.680
Good news for purists: the new Child's Play
production reportedly uses a total of six

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:18.810
animatronic Chucky dolls, operated by three
to four puppeteers at a time.

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:21.569
In a behind-the-scenes video, producer David
Katzenberg said:

00:04:21.569 --> 00:04:25.860
"A big part of getting Chucky right was having
animatronics be a lot of the times that we

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:26.500
see Chucky."

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:29.740
Details about the new movie are pretty slim
right now.

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:34.000
By all accounts, Child's Play is a straightforward
horror flick without a whole lot of room for

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:34.500
comedy.

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:38.320
That said, if things do get weird, it'd be
far from a first for Chucky.

00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:42.020
While the first three Child's Play movies
were fairly straight-faced thrillers, Bride

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:46.120
of Chucky came along in 1998 and took the
series in a campy new direction.

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:48.720
Things got increasingly bizarre from there.

00:04:48.740 --> 00:04:52.860
That same year, Chucky appeared on Saturday
Night Live's Weekend Update segment with Colin

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:53.360
Quinn.

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:56.800
"Well I think I speak for most Americans when
I say, 'Enough already.'"

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:02.599
Chucky also quite memorably hijacked a WCW
wrestling broadcast, and then there was that

00:05:02.599 --> 00:05:04.050
interview with Entertainment Weekly.

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:07.200
"You really wanna know if I have a 'Tickle
Me' function?

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:09.840
Push here, dipstick, and see what happens."

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:15.100
Most recently, he made a highly memorable
cameo in 2018's Ready Player One.

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:19.240
The point is, the strangest thing would be
if the new Chucky didn't get strange.

